	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "nxNervLlx4Hv28Uhe",
			"markdown": "Ambush Strike: The Stalker gets +2 to attack when attacking from concealment and gains a bonus to its first attack if the target has not detected it. It should preferentially attack the character with the lowest DR—probably CyberPixie or the Mage—rather than charging the Pilot."
		},
		{
			"id": "nzS1XcKhMsq6WVYlo",
			"markdown": "Refraction:The creature's skin contains microscopic crystalline structures that manipulate light and infrared radiation.\n\nWhen stationary:\n\n Vision-based Sense rolls to detect it are at -6.\n\n When moving slowly: -3.\n\nIt doesn't disappear. Someone who knows where to look can see something is wrong.\n\nA successful Perception roll with the appropriate sensor can detect it.\n\nThe important thing is that the players can defeat this.\n\nThe Mage's magic, particularly Sound, Seek Water, environmental manipulation, etc., can potentially help them locate it.\n\nThe Jack's Combat Sense is also useful here."
		}
	],
